  "notes": "Coordinates in daniela_master_padded.png pixels (1152x1332). Layers back-to-front: 'tail' (static for now; its own joint comes later) and 'main'. Separating the tail removes the 4-15 px cheek/tail gap from the head's bend zone, so the bend there only stretches transparent space. The tail region hugs the tail's left silhouette (measured row by row from alpha); faint right-whisker strokes over the tail stay with the tail. Rigid head includes ears, whiskers and jaw outline (cut ~12 px below it); the white neck is the bend zone. Tail layer has a 'tail' joint: base anchored behind the back, curl rigid, bend through the middle. Front legs: paw_*_reach rotate from the shoulder (overlay on, leg drawn over haunch/chest); paw_*_lift use a far pivot at paw height so small angles lift the paw almost vertically (left: negative = up, right: positive = up). Leg zones measured from the outline strokes row by row.",
